 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "`active_app`, `g` and `request` are context-local proxies onto a single `ContextVar`.\n\n- **Mechanism:** `src/tessel/globals.py` defines a `_app_var` `ContextVar`. `active_app`, `g`, `request`, `session` and `app_ctx` are werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects that read from it. Each proxy resolves, at access time, to an attribute of whichever `AppContext` is currently pushed in the calling thread or async context.\n- **Object they resolve through:** `AppContext` in `src/tessel/ctx.py`. There is one per request or CLI command, and `has_request` says whether it carries a request. It replaces the old split between a request context and an app context, and `RequestContext` is now only a deprecated alias.\n- **What each proxy returns from the current context:**\n  - `active_app` is the `Tessel` app instance (`src/tessel/app.py`).\n  - `g` is the instance of the app's `app_ctx_globals_class`.\n  - `request` is a `Request` from `src/tessel/wrappers.py`.\n\nI answered from `brain/architecture.md` and did not open the source files.",
